  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Three grips, one triad. Root position, first inversion, and second inversion on strings 1-2-3 are the same three notes, rotated so a different one lands on the bottom each time. Meet them in the order your hand actually finds them climbing the neck, and three things to memorise turn into one thing happening three times — the same C, E, and G, just taking turns at the bottom."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lowest of the three sits right at the nut: second inversion, the fifth in the bass."
        }
      ]
    },
