    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Laid end to end, the three grips are a single climb: second inversion, root position, first inversion, each one a few frets past the last. The diagram below draws that whole climb on strings 1-2-3 at once, labeled band by band, all the way up the neck — including where it repeats. It has no play button; its job is showing the shape of the climb, not the sound of any one grip. Nothing new to learn here — it's the same three grips from above, just seen end to end instead of one at a time."
        }
      ]
    },
